- @frontend/core/accessibility.mdc for accessibility testing

## Overview
This document defines the rules and best practices for testing Ruby on Rails frontend applications.

## Testing Principles

### 1. Test Types
- System Tests: Test complete user flows with Capybara
- Integration Tests: Test controller actions and views
- Feature Tests: Test specific features
- View Tests: Test view templates
- Accessibility Tests: Test a11y compliance

### 2. Test Organization
- Group tests by feature
- Use descriptive test names
- Follow RSpec best practices
- Keep tests independent
- Maintain test isolation

### 3. Test Coverage
- Aim for meaningful coverage
- Focus on critical paths
- Test edge cases
- Test error scenarios
- Test accessibility

## Implementation Guidelines

### System Tests
```ruby
# Good
RSpec.describe "User management", type: :system do
  it "allows user to update their profile" do
    sign_in user
    visit edit_user_path(user)
    
    fill_in "Name", with: "New Name"
    click_button "Update Profile"
    
    expect(page).to have_content "Profile updated successfully"
    expect(page).to have_content "New Name"
  end
end

# Bad
RSpec.describe "Everything", type: :system do
  it "works" do
    # Unclear test purpose
    # Mixed concerns
    # No clear assertions
  end
end
```

### View Tests
```ruby
# Good
RSpec.describe "users/show", type: :view do
  it "displays user information" do
    assign(:user, build_stubbed(:user, name: "John Doe"))
    render
    
    expect(rendered).to have_content "John Doe"
    expect(rendered).to have_link "Edit Profile"
  end
end
```

## Testing Tools
- RSpec for testing framework
- Capybara for system tests
- FactoryBot for test data
- Faker for test data generation
- Axe for accessibility testing

## Performance Testing
- Load time testing
- Database query testing
- Cache effectiveness testing
- Asset loading testing
- Memory usage testing

## Common Mistakes to Avoid
- Not using proper test data
- Not cleaning up test data
- Not testing error scenarios
- Not testing accessibility
- Not testing edge cases

## Validation Checklist
- [ ] System tests implemented
- [ ] Integration tests implemented
- [ ] View tests implemented
- [ ] Accessibility tests implemented
- [ ] Test coverage meets requirements
- [ ] Tests are maintainable
- [ ] Tests are independent
- [ ] Test data is properly managed
